# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own Supabase project's values.
# Find both under Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API.
#
# Both of these are safe to ship inside the app bundle: the "anon"/"publishable"
# key is designed to be public and is only ever as powerful as the RLS policies
# on each table allow (Claude-Context.md Section 5.3). The Supabase
# service-role key and the Razorpay secret key must NEVER go in this file or
# anywhere under app/, components/, features/, or lib/ — they belong only in
# Supabase Edge Function environment variables, starting Phase 4/5.
#
# Must be prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ — that's what tells Expo to inline a variable
# into the app bundle. Anything without that prefix (e.g. NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which
# is a Next.js convention, not an Expo one) is invisible to this app.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key
